# syntax=ghcr.io/hyper-light/shards
#
# A shards microVM that applies a slates VFS over shards' NATIVE virtio-fs backend (§4.6, the slates integration).
# The guest mounts a slates volume by its virtio-fs tag `shards0` — no kernel NFS, no host mount, no 9p. slates'
# `bridge-fuse` `shards_fs::serve` is the backend; it speaks the same le32-length + FUSE framing shards' fs device
# speaks (`Slot::ask`/`write_frame`/`read_frame`), so the device, pointed at a slates daemon's socket, reaches the
# volume directly.
#
# DAX compatibility: the slates side IS DAX-capable (the device DAX window — FUSE SETUPMAPPING over a pinned
# arena block — is built and hardened; see ../../wip/SLATES_DESIGN.md §4.6 and the [[dax-mapping-gate]] memory). The
# shards microVM gets the NON-DAX FUSE path here, because shards' fs device has no guest-physical DAX cache window
# yet; when it gains one, the same backend serves SETUPMAPPING and the guest reaches the block through its own page
# table. So "DAX-compatible" = the backend supports DAX; the microVM is accelerated once shards adds the window.
#
# STATUS of the directive below: the `SLATES` line is the INTENDED high-level packaging. It is NOT yet a shards
# Agentfile directive — the daemon-side wiring (connect to the slates socket, hand the descriptor to the VM's fs
# share slot, as the daemon already does for its share process) is the shards-side follow-up. The WORKING mechanism
# today is the low-level `run --kernel … --slates-fs-fd <N>` flag, which this repo builds and proves end to end
# (slates `crates/bridge-fuse`; shards `crates/shards/src/vm_run.rs` + `crates/shards/tests/slates_fs.rs`). See
# README.md for the full runnable recipe.

FROM alpine:3.22

# Mount a slates volume, served by a slates daemon on SLATES_SOCK, at tag `shards0` -> /slates.
# (Proposed directive; today this is `--slates-fs-fd <N>`, the daemon filling the share slot from the socket.)
SLATES ${SLATES_SOCK} shards0 /slates

# Hand off to the workload once the slates volume is mounted.
ENTRYPOINT ["/bin/sh", "-c", "mount -t virtiofs shards0 /slates && exec \"$@\"", "--"]
CMD ["cat", "/slates/hello"]
